WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.834
Contrastive self-supervised learning has
transformed computer vision by training networks

00:00:03.914 --> 00:00:07.749
on huge pools of unlabeled data to produce
embeddings that transfer well to downstream

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:11.663
tasks.

00:00:11.743 --> 00:00:15.578
It has worked for natural images and medical images,

00:00:15.658 --> 00:00:19.492
but has rarely been applied to remote sensing.

00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:23.407
That gap matters here,

00:00:23.487 --> 00:00:27.321
because Sentinel-1 alone collects roughly a hundred
and twenty thousand Wave-mode ocean images every single month.

00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:31.236
This study tests the hypothesis that contrastive
learning on that unlabeled stream can

00:00:31.316 --> 00:00:35.150
overcome the scarcity of expert labels for SAR analysis.
